# Code Patterns & Style Guide

## Code Standards & Architecture Patterns

### Method Naming Conventions
- **User Instance Methods**: Clearly indicate they return user-provided data
  - ❌ `fn first_term()` - Misleading (suggests term character)
  - ✅ `fn get_user_instance_at(position: usize)` - Clear intent
  - ✅ `/// Get user instance at position 0 (maps to canonical "Will")`
  
**See Also**: 
- [Backend Terminology Rules](mdc:.cursor/rules/backend-terminology.mdc) for comprehensive backend patterns
- [Frontend Terminology Rules](mdc:.cursor/rules/frontend-terminology.mdc) for frontend consistency

### Documentation Standards
Method comments must distinguish between:
- **User data access**: What the user provided
- **Canonical term mapping**: What it represents in Bennett's system  
- **Positional coordinates**: Array indices and geometric positions

```rust
/// Get user instance at position 0 (maps to canonical "Will")
/// Returns the user-provided term for the first position of the triad
fn get_user_instance_at(&self, position: usize) -> Option<&str>
```

### Terminology Consistency
- **User instances**: Terms provided by users (stored in database)
- **Canonical terms**: Reference terms from Bennett's framework
- **Term characters**: Library method name for term characters
- **Positional mapping**: Clear indication of user→canonical mapping

### API Structure Organization
- Structure files in `api/src/structures/` should follow consistent patterns
- Each structure implements the same trait interface
- Source attribution metadata included in all structures
- Canonical terms fetched from library, not hardcoded

### Frontend Architecture Patterns
- **No Hardcoded Terms**: Always fetch term characters from API
- **API-First**: Use `/schema/{structure_type}` endpoint for dynamic terms
- **Separation of Concerns**: Positioning logic separate from data fetching
- **Error States**: Proper loading/error/incomplete state handling

## Implementation Patterns

### Structure Implementation Template
```rust
use crate::structures::SystematicStructure;
use library::bennett::{StructureName, StructureError};

impl SystematicStructure for StructureName {
    fn term_characters(&self) -> Vec<String> {
        // Fetch from library, never hardcode
        self.get_term_characters()
    }
    
    fn get_user_instance_at(&self, position: usize) -> Option<&str> {
        // Clear method naming
        self.instances.get(position)
    }
}
```

### Error Handling Patterns
```rust
// Use Result types consistently
fn process_structure(data: &str) -> Result<Structure, StructureError> {
    // Validate input
    // Process with proper error context
    // Return meaningful errors
}
```

### Frontend Component Patterns
```rust
// API-driven components
impl Component for SystemOverlay {
    fn view(&self, ctx: &Context<Self>) -> Html {
        if self.loading_schema {
            return self.render_loading_state();
        }
        
        if self.schema.is_none() {
            return self.render_error_state();
        }
        
        self.render_with_api_data()
    }
}
```

## Code Review Checklist

### Backend (Rust)
- [ ] Method names clearly indicate user vs canonical data
- [ ] Comments distinguish between user instances and term characters
- [ ] No hardcoded term characters anywhere
- [ ] Proper error handling with meaningful messages
- [ ] Consistent trait implementations across structures
- [ ] Source attribution metadata present

### Frontend (Yew)
- [ ] No hardcoded term characters in components
- [ ] API calls used for all term character references
- [ ] Proper loading/error state handling
- [ ] Positioning logic separated from data fetching
- [ ] Responsive design considerations

### API Design
- [ ] RESTful endpoint design
- [ ] Consistent response formats
- [ ] Proper HTTP status codes
- [ ] Schema endpoints for dynamic data
- [ ] Input validation and sanitization

